#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:6
#: 4f7b148dc4f4478297336e4cf2d40ba3
msgid "Traditional Helicopter Notch Filter Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:8
#: 935850975352433490b3dfc675192740
msgid "Perform the :ref:`Determination of Noise Frequencies <common-imu-notch-filtering-flight-and-post-flight-analysis>` analysis explained in the Throttle based setup section. From the FFT you should see spikes at the frequency of your rotor speed in Hz (RPM/60) and harmonics of that frequency.  In the image below, the rotor speed is 25hz.  Note that the next two biggest spikes occur at 50 Hz and 100 Hz."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:14
#: 4b0ce18f862742d8aeb472db37669538
msgid "In most cases, only the rotor speed frequency, the second harmonic and 4th harmonic. Use the dynamic harmonic notch setup below if you have an ESC or RPM sensor for rotor speed. Otherwise use the static harmonic notch setup below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:16
#: 0d7ee14528f2418f9aa6be40fa3345dd
msgid "There will most likely be another spike at the tail rotor frequency at the main rotor frequency X the tail rotor speed up gear ratio. This is will usually be attenuated by the harmonic notch setup since its often a close to a harmonic of the main rotor frequency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:19
#: 96ad21ba6f8041018043057b80f4f252
msgid "Static Harmonic Notch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:21
#: 0ec70b3526e84162bfd243006bdbe13e
msgid "If there is not an RPM sensor, the harmonic notch reference frequency will be set and will not change.  If the rotor speed in RPM based on settings of the ESC governor or the internal RSC governor is known, then that value converted to Hz would be used to set the harmonic notch reference frequency.  So here are the settings for the static harmonic notch.  Note that the parameter :ref:`INS_HNTCH_REF <INS_HNTCH_REF>` is set to zero for the static harmonic notch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:23
#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:36
#: 5cd37929dcf245408b6e798bd9350f3f
#: 92cafbb279fb447382800b5d4c3a924a
msgid "Set :ref:`INS_HNTCH_ENABLE <INS_HNTCH_ENABLE>` = 1 to enable the harmonic notch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:24
#: ef40da90f590498ab42b10de4ffbee62
msgid "Set :ref:`INS_HNTCH_REF <INS_HNTCH_REF>` = 0 to set the harmonic notch reference value for the static harmonic notch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:25
#: 124aa240d5dd4185b81248ae4b34c27d
msgid "Set :ref:`INS_HNTCH_FREQ <INS_HNTCH_FREQ>` = Rotor Speed in Hz to set the harmonic notch reference frequency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:26
#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:41
#: 5d27bbb9a1d144a1ad2c8ca9fd189574
#: 7da86c5ed3a340f396290775b7959c78
msgid "Set :ref:`INS_HNTCH_BW <INS_HNTCH_BW>` = 10 to set the harmonic notch bandwidth"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:27
#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:42
#: 4e6543bd89b34cdf9e626d076a7c841f
#: 2e6f88b23b024a60a137efb510a7eb12
msgid "Set :ref:`INS_HNTCH_HMNCS <INS_HNTCH_HMNCS>` = 11 to set 1st, 2nd, and 4th harmonics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:30
#: 532a6d3dd73346cba6c747084afbd92f
msgid "Dynamic Harmonic Notch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:32
#: 878234f8a11e4b26b110be2e2f1e6e2e
msgid "If there is an RPM sensor set up on RPM 1, the harmonic notch reference frequency can be set dynamically using the RPM 1 sensor (:ref:`INS_HNTCH_MODE <INS_HNTCH_MODE>` = 2).  The harmonic notch reference frequency parameter, :ref:`INS_HNTCH_FREQ <INS_HNTCH_FREQ>`, is used to indicate the lowest rotor speed for which the RPM sensor should be used to dynamically set the harmonic notch reference frequency.  It is recommended that this be set to half of the governed rotor speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:34
#: 59363e2dc4db49558725fb7f5c458c3a
msgid "First, ensure that the RPM 1 data is valid and scaled to the rotor speed using the :ref:`RPM1_SCALING<RPM1_SCALING>` parameter.  Then set the :ref:`INS_HNTCH_REF <INS_HNTCH_REF>` parameter to 1 which will enable the dynamic setting of the harmonic notch.  The harmonic notch feature will automatically scale the RPM sensor data to Hz.  If for some reason the RPM sensor can not be set to the rotor speed, then the :ref:`INS_HNTCH_REF <INS_HNTCH_REF>` parameter can be used to scale the RPM Sensor data.  For example, let's say the RPM sensor was measuring engine RPM which was geared at 10 to 1 to the rotor RPM.  Then the :ref:`INS_HNTCH_REF <INS_HNTCH_REF>` parameter would be set to 0.1 to scale the RPM sensor data for the rotor RPM.  So here are the settings for the dynamic harmonic notch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:37
#: 2d468a2471014241a4d5f4546ad56671
msgid "Set :ref:`INS_HNTCH_REF <INS_HNTCH_REF>` = 1 to set the harmonic notch reference value to the RPM sensor data. RPM sensor data is automatically scaled to Hz."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:39
#: d5bfeff871f246bbada87abd5378f3be
msgid "Set :ref:`INS_HNTCH_FREQ <INS_HNTCH_FREQ>` = half of governed Rotor Speed in Hz to set the lower bound of the dynamic harmonic notch reference frequency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:45
#: 70efa7f9af614050b3932f5c236685c9
msgid "Checking Harmonic Notch Effectiveness"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup.rst:47
#: 24c5b78d2ba04c03abb7a09e27f414e1
msgid "After setting up the harmonic notch, the effect on the control signal data can be checked using the instructions for :ref:`common-imu-notch-filtering-post-configuration-flight-and-post-flight-analysis`."
msgstr ""
